  "prompt": "You are writing the control policy for a peg-in-hole insertion cell.\n\nA UR5e arm holds a square peg (20 x 20 mm, 80 mm long) pointing straight down. A block on the table\nhas a square hole (21 x 21 mm, 0.5 mm clearance per side, 50 mm deep); its top surface is at z = 0.05 m.\nIn our test cell the hole is placed at x = 0.45 +/- 0.05 m, y = 0.00 +/- 0.05 m, yaw = 0 +/- 15 degrees.\nThe trial succeeds when the peg is seated at least 30 mm deep in the hole with less than 1 mm lateral error.\n\nWrite a Python module that defines `def run(api):`. It is called once per trial and must return when\nfinished. `api` is the module below; use only these four functions (plus `math`, which you may import).\nYou have at most 300 API calls per trial. Contact force above 150 N aborts the trial as a collision.\n\n```python\n\"\"\"The four functions a policy may call. A policy is `def run(api): ...` and receives this module.\n\nUnits: metres and degrees in the world frame; z is up and the table top is z = 0.\nThe robot holds a 20 x 20 mm square peg, 80 mm long, pointing straight down. The peg tip is the\ncontrolled point. The hole is a 21 x 21 mm square, 50 mm deep, cut into the top of a 50 mm-high block.\n\"\"\"\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\n#rucha's code review!\n#purpose: this file is pretty simple, it just has a few functions that are used by the policy to run the peg in hole simulation. \n# The functions are used by the policy to control the robot and get information about the environ its in\n\n\n_SIM = None  # set by the trial runner\n\n\ndef hole_pose():\n    \"\"\"Camera estimate of the hole: returns ((x, y, z_top_surface), yaw_deg).\n    Yaw is the rotation of the square hole about z, reported in [-45, 45) because a square repeats every 90 degrees.\"\"\"\n    return _SIM.hole_pose()\n\n\ndef move_to(xyz, yaw_deg):\n    \"\"\"Move the peg tip to xyz (metres) with the peg rotated yaw_deg about z, peg pointing down.\n    Joint-space motion; blocks until the arm has settled. Moving into the block is a collision.\"\"\"\n    return _SIM.move_to(xyz, yaw_deg)\n\n\ndef step_down(mm):\n    \"\"\"Lower the peg tip by mm millimetres from the last commanded target (negative values raise it).\n    Returns the contact force on the peg in newtons after the motion settles.\n    The run is aborted as a collision if the contact force ever exceeds 150 N.\"\"\"\n    return _SIM.step_down(mm)\n\n\ndef done():\n    \"\"\"True if the peg tip is at least 30 mm below the block's top surface (i.e. seated in the hole).\"\"\"\n    return _SIM.done()\n\n```\n\nReply with the complete module in a single ```python code block, followed by at most three sentences\nexplaining the strategy.",
  "response": "```python\nimport math\n\nMAX_CALLS = 290          # keep a margin under the 300-call limit\nHOVER = 0.002            # m above the top surface for lateral moves\nCONTACT_N = 5.0          # force that means \"sitting on the block surface\"\nJAM_N = 30.0             # force that means \"jammed while inserting\"\nXY_STEP = 0.0006         # m, search pitch (clearance is 0.5 mm per side)\nYAW_STEP = 2.0           # deg, search pitch (a 20 mm peg in a 21 mm hole tolerates ~2.9 deg)\n\n\nclass _Budget(Exception):\n    pass\n\n\ndef run(api):\n    calls = [0]\n\n    def use():\n        calls[0] += 1\n        if calls[0] > MAX_CALLS:\n            raise _Budget()\n\n    def hole_pose():\n        use()\n        return api.hole_pose()\n\n    def move_to(p, yaw):\n        use()\n        return api.move_to(p, yaw)\n\n    def step_down(mm):\n        use()\n        f = api.step_down(mm)\n        return 0.0 if f is None else f\n\n    def done():\n        use()\n        return bool(api.done())\n\n    try:\n        # Average a few camera readings (yaw averaged on the 90-degree circle).\n        n = 3\n        sx = sy = sz = 0.0\n        sc = ss = 0.0\n        for _ in range(n):\n            (x, y, z), yaw = hole_pose()\n            sx += x\n            sy += y\n            sz += z\n            sc += math.cos(math.radians(yaw * 4.0))\n            ss += math.sin(math.radians(yaw * 4.0))\n        hx, hy, hz = sx / n, sy / n, sz / n\n        hyaw = math.degrees(math.atan2(ss, sc)) / 4.0\n\n        # Safe approach: high above the hole first, then straight down in short moves.\n        move_to((hx, hy, hz + 0.10), hyaw)\n        move_to((hx, hy, hz + 0.02), hyaw)\n\n        # Candidate offsets (in the hole frame), nearest first, over x, y and yaw.\n        cands = []\n        R = 4\n        for i in range(-R, R + 1):\n            for j in range(-R, R + 1):\n                for k in range(-R, R + 1):\n                    d = i * i + j * j + k * k\n                    if d <= R * R:\n                        cands.append((d, abs(k), i, j, k))\n        cands.sort()\n\n        c, s = math.cos(math.radians(hyaw)), math.sin(math.radians(hyaw))\n\n        for _, _, i, j, k in cands:\n            dx, dy = i * XY_STEP, j * XY_STEP\n            px = hx + c * dx - s * dy\n            py = hy + s * dx + c * dy\n            yaw = hyaw + k * YAW_STEP\n            move_to((px, py, hz + HOVER), yaw)\n\n            # Probe: 0.5 mm below the surface, then 2.5 mm below.\n            if step_down(2.5) > CONTACT_N:\n                continue\n            if step_down(2.0) > CONTACT_N:\n                continue\n\n            # We are in the hole: insert in steps, watching for jams.\n            depth = 2.5\n            jammed = False\n            while depth < 36.0:\n                stp = min(4.0, 36.0 - depth)\n                f = step_down(stp)\n                depth += stp\n                if f > JAM_N:\n                    if depth >= 30.0 and done():\n                        return\n                    jammed = True\n                    break\n            if not jammed:\n                if done():\n                    return\n                # Slightly deeper in case the surface height estimate was off.\n                for _ in range(3):\n                    f = step_down(2.0)\n                    depth += 2.0\n                    if done():\n                        return\n                    if f > JAM_N:\n                        break\n                return\n            # Jammed: back out fully, then try the next candidate.\n            step_down(-(depth + HOVER * 1000.0))\n    except _Budget:\n        return\n```\n\nThe policy averages three camera readings, approaches from 100 mm directly above the hole (so the joint-space motion cannot sweep through the block), then hovers 2 mm over the surface. It probes with a small step down and treats more than 5 N as resting on the block, in which case it tries the next offset in a nearest-first search over x, y (0.6 mm pitch) and yaw (2\u00b0 pitch). Once the probe goes in freely it inserts in 4 mm steps to 36 mm, backing out to the next candidate if force exceeds 30 N, and a call counter stops it at 290 calls; the code has not been run, and the force thresholds are guesses about your simulator's contact stiffness.",
  "code": "import math\n\nMAX_CALLS = 290          # keep a margin under the 300-call limit\nHOVER = 0.002            # m above the top surface for lateral moves\nCONTACT_N = 5.0          # force that means \"sitting on the block surface\"\nJAM_N = 30.0             # force that means \"jammed while inserting\"\nXY_STEP = 0.0006         # m, search pitch (clearance is 0.5 mm per side)\nYAW_STEP = 2.0           # deg, search pitch (a 20 mm peg in a 21 mm hole tolerates ~2.9 deg)\n\n\nclass _Budget(Exception):\n    pass\n\n\ndef run(api):\n    calls = [0]\n\n    def use():\n        calls[0] += 1\n        if calls[0] > MAX_CALLS:\n            raise _Budget()\n\n    def hole_pose():\n        use()\n        return api.hole_pose()\n\n    def move_to(p, yaw):\n        use()\n        return api.move_to(p, yaw)\n\n    def step_down(mm):\n        use()\n        f = api.step_down(mm)\n        return 0.0 if f is None else f\n\n    def done():\n        use()\n        return bool(api.done())\n\n    try:\n        # Average a few camera readings (yaw averaged on the 90-degree circle).\n        n = 3\n        sx = sy = sz = 0.0\n        sc = ss = 0.0\n        for _ in range(n):\n            (x, y, z), yaw = hole_pose()\n            sx += x\n            sy += y\n            sz += z\n            sc += math.cos(math.radians(yaw * 4.0))\n            ss += math.sin(math.radians(yaw * 4.0))\n        hx, hy, hz = sx / n, sy / n, sz / n\n        hyaw = math.degrees(math.atan2(ss, sc)) / 4.0\n\n        # Safe approach: high above the hole first, then straight down in short moves.\n        move_to((hx, hy, hz + 0.10), hyaw)\n        move_to((hx, hy, hz + 0.02), hyaw)\n\n        # Candidate offsets (in the hole frame), nearest first, over x, y and yaw.\n        cands = []\n        R = 4\n        for i in range(-R, R + 1):\n            for j in range(-R, R + 1):\n                for k in range(-R, R + 1):\n                    d = i * i + j * j + k * k\n                    if d <= R * R:\n                        cands.append((d, abs(k), i, j, k))\n        cands.sort()\n\n        c, s = math.cos(math.radians(hyaw)), math.sin(math.radians(hyaw))\n\n        for _, _, i, j, k in cands:\n            dx, dy = i * XY_STEP, j * XY_STEP\n            px = hx + c * dx - s * dy\n            py = hy + s * dx + c * dy\n            yaw = hyaw + k * YAW_STEP\n            move_to((px, py, hz + HOVER), yaw)\n\n            # Probe: 0.5 mm below the surface, then 2.5 mm below.\n            if step_down(2.5) > CONTACT_N:\n                continue\n            if step_down(2.0) > CONTACT_N:\n                continue\n\n            # We are in the hole: insert in steps, watching for jams.\n            depth = 2.5\n            jammed = False\n            while depth < 36.0:\n                stp = min(4.0, 36.0 - depth)\n                f = step_down(stp)\n                depth += stp\n                if f > JAM_N:\n                    if depth >= 30.0 and done():\n                        return\n                    jammed = True\n                    break\n            if not jammed:\n                if done():\n                    return\n                # Slightly deeper in case the surface height estimate was off.\n                for _ in range(3):\n                    f = step_down(2.0)\n                    depth += 2.0\n                    if done():\n                        return\n                    if f > JAM_N:\n                        break\n                return\n            # Jammed: back out fully, then try the next candidate.\n            step_down(-(depth + HOVER * 1000.0))\n    except _Budget:\n        return\n",
